          "verdict": "malicious",
          "category": "code_insight",
          "analysis": "The sample is an ARM-based DDoS bot. It daemonizes itself by forking, then connects to a Command and Control (C2) server to receive commands. The `processCmd` function parses these commands to initiate various network flood attacks, including 'OVH', 'STD', 'UDPRAW', and 'RANDHEX'. It contains a large list of hardcoded User-Agent strings to spoof HTTP requests during Layer 7 attacks, evident in functions like `SendHTTPHex` and `sendHTTPtwo`. The binary also performs local network reconnaissance by reading `/proc/net/route` and `/etc/resolv.conf`. A clear IOC is the botnet-related URL `http://www[.]billybobbot[.]com/crawler/` found in its strings.",
          "id": "48b36bab43fb248727c6e8da4ab8d0affc1bc59c9238542467c4f98c1b42f31e-file-palm"
